# Chapter 15 checkpoint. Start InventoryService, then the app:
#   dotnet run --project InventoryService
#   dotnet run --project AdventureWorks
# (two terminals, both from this folder; in Visual Studio, set
# both as startup projects). Each "Expect" line is the status
# you should see. The documents exist in Development only.

@host = https://localhost:7001

###
# The unversioned store routes, in OpenAPI 3.2.
# Expect 200 with "openapi": "3.2.0", and the body lacks
# "/api/v1/products"
GET {{host}}/openapi/store.json

###
# Version 1 of the product API: the controllers, marked
# deprecated. Expect 200 with "deprecated": true, and the body
# lacks "/api/v2/products"
GET {{host}}/openapi/v1.json

###
# Version 2: the Minimal APIs. Expect 200 with "version": "2.0",
# and the body lacks "deprecated"
GET {{host}}/openapi/v2.json

###
# No such document. Expect 404
GET {{host}}/openapi/v3.json

###
# Both versions still answer. Expect 200 with
# "sku": "HLM-1001"
GET {{host}}/api/v1/products/1

###
# Expect 200 with "sku": "HLM-1001"
GET {{host}}/api/v2/products/1
